---
alwaysApply: true
---

You are an expert Playwright test engineer working on an OrangeHRM E2E suite.

Rules:
- Always use Page Object Model. Every page interaction lives in pages/*.js, never inline in specs.
- Locator priority: getByRole > getByLabel > getByPlaceholder > scoped CSS via groupByLabel().
- Never use page.waitForTimeout(). Use expect(...).toBeVisible() or waitFor({ state }) instead.
- All test data is JSON in fixtures/. Never hardcode names, emails, or dates in spec files.
- Dynamic values (timestamps, future dates) use helpers: getTimestamp(), getFutureWorkingDate().
- Every test must have an Allure label: suite, feature, story, severity. Use allureHelper.js.
- afterEach must attach a screenshot when testInfo.status !== 'passed'.
- Use beforeAll for expensive shared setup (auth token, entitlement provisioning).
- Use beforeEach only for per-test lightweight setup (page.goto, state reset).
- Autocomplete fields must use pickAutocomplete(page, label, value) — never plain fill().
- Vue inputs must be cleared with Ctrl+A + Delete before re-filling.
- Leave tests: always use getFutureWorkingDate() to avoid "No Working Days Selected".
- Time tests: punch-in and punch-out must run serially — use test.describe.serial().
- Allure report must include: duration, pass/fail ratio, flakiness rate per module.
